        "original_id": "663da274-cf76-5c1c-9ddb-5dd28df76db2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Beaulieu Mine, Yellowknife, Northwest Territories\n- Companies: McIntyre Mines\n- Topics: gold mining, copper production, post-World War II mining\n\nFacts:\n- The Beaulieu Mine was a post-World War II gold mining operation near Yellowknife, Northwest Territories.\n- The Beaulieu Mine entered production in October 1947.\n- By the end of November 1947, the Beaulieu Mine had recovered only 7 troy ounces (220 g) of rough gold.\n- McIntyre Mines yielded a considerable amount of copper over its operating life.",
